# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: native-and-dotnet-plugins — load application DLLs (C ABI and .NET [LispFunction] assemblies such as EPURELIB) into clautolisp
#+STATUS: DEFERRED
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: epic
#+DEPENDS: cador-multidocument-host (document reopen), a study phase (below)
#+BRANCH: feature-native-and-dotnet-plugins
#+DATE: 2026-10-05

* Context

pjb, 2026-10-05: "Concerning the application specific DLLs
(dotnet/BricsCAD/EPURELIB.dll dotnet/AutoCAD/EPURELIB.dll, sources in
EPURELIB), what would be required from clautolisp if we wanted to compile a
DLL loadable in clautolisp to use these functions implemented in C#?" -- then:
"Write a deferred epic for the whole thing (we still need to study it, and
notably if we want to support windows API, like COM and other dependencies
on windows for C# code)."

The case: SCHMS+ (~pjb/src/fabrik/schms/) ships EPURELIB, ~4600 lines of C#
(EPURELIB/EPURELIB.csproj), built twice from one source -- Framework=AutoCAD
(AcCoreMgd / AcDbMgd / AcMgd 2022, #if ARX_APP) and Framework=BricsCAD
(BrxMgd / TD_Mgd V25, #if BRX_APP) -- TargetFramework net48, UseWindowsForms,
Costura.Fody-embedded dependencies (DocumentFormat.OpenXml, RestSharp,
System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt, OuranosClient). The CAD loads it with
(command-s "._netload" path) from SCHMS+'s charge_dll.lsp; EPUREE's
replacement skips the netload off Windows (epuree/post-deploy/schmsplus/
src-vlx/charge_dll.lsp), so those call sites fail on macOS / Linux, and
under clautolisp everywhere.

Today clautolisp has NO plugin loading: ARXLOAD / ARX / AUTOARXLOAD /
VL-ARX-IMPORT are nil stubs, there is no NETLOAD, and vlax-create-object only
reaches cador's mock ProgID table (no real Windows COM; only the wire host
forwards to a real CAD's COM server).

* What EPURELIB uses (inventory, 2026-10-05)

18 [LispFunction]s + 1 [CommandMethod]:

| function(s)                                                     | needs beyond marshalling                         |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------+--------------------------------------------------|
| get_new_guid, nombre_aleatoire, Add, DivMod, HttpGet,           | nothing (pure .NET)                              |
| parse_condition_itineraire                                      |                                                  |
| ouranos_get_refgeo, ouranos_get_postes, ouranos_lake_upload     | network + RestSharp/JWT (pure .NET)              |
| schms_generer_rapport_verification                              | OpenXml (pure .NET); PDF via Word COM interop    |
|                                                                 | (Windows + Word installed)                       |
| ouvre_liste_edit, actu_liste_edit                               | Editor.SelectAll(filter: INSERT + xdata app),    |
|                                                                 | Transaction.GetObject, GetXDataForApplication,   |
|                                                                 | WinForms                                         |
| ouvre_suivi_modif, ouvre_editeur_voies, ouvre_condit,           | WinForms (Application.ShowModalDialog)           |
| vers_presse_papiers                                             |                                                  |
| schms_reouvrir_lecture_seule (+ SCHMS_REOUVRIR_LECTURE_SEULE_EXEC) | DocumentCollection.Open(path, readOnly),     |
|                                                                 | CloseAndDiscard, IsReadOnly, SendStringToExecute |

Also, throughout: ResultBuffer / TypedValue / LispDataType (182 TypedValue
uses: Text, Int16, Int32, Double, Nil, T, ListBegin / ListEnd / DottedPair),
LISP callbacks from C# (Application.Invoke / Bricscad.Global.Editor.Invoke),
SendStringToExecute (9 uses: deferred commands cmd_set_suivi_modif,
schms_image_depose, cmd_set_cadres, ...), Editor.WriteMessage.

* Proposal (three layers -- to be confirmed by the study)

1. *A native plugin ABI (language-neutral), the ADS layer.* C entry points
   exported by clautolisp through CFFI callbacks, plus a loader:
   - register a LISP-callable function / a command (acedDefun-like; the
     command reuses vlax-add-cmd's path);
   - resbuf marshalling AutoLISP <-> a linked list of (type-code . value),
     with LispDataType's codes (5001 real, 5002 2D point, 5003 short, 5005
     string, 5006 ename, 5007 pickset, 5009 3D point, 5010 long, 5014 void,
     5016 list begin, 5017 list end, 5018 dotted pair, 5019 nil, 5021 T);
   - call back into LISP (acedInvoke-like; the evaluator must allow nested
     calls from foreign code);
   - drawing services on handles: ssget with a filter, entget / entmod
     incl. xdata, prompt / write-message;
   - a deferred command queue (SendStringToExecute: run after the current
     LISP call returns).
   Useful without .NET: C / C++ / Rust / C#-NativeAOT plugins on every OS.
2. *.NET hosting.* hostfxr / nethost (.NET 8, Windows / macOS / Linux) via
   CFFI; or, Windows only, mscoree CLR hosting for unmodified net48
   assemblies. A NETLOAD builtin (and (command "._netload" path)) that loads
   the assembly, reflects on [LispFunction] / [CommandMethod] and registers
   them through layer 1.
3. *A managed shim of the CAD API subset above* -- ResultBuffer, TypedValue,
   LispDataType, DxfCode, ObjectId, Transaction, OpenMode, Entity
   (GetXDataForApplication), Editor (SelectAll, SelectionFilter,
   PromptStatus, WriteMessage, Invoke), Application (DocumentManager,
   MdiActiveDocument, SendStringToExecute, ShowModalDialog), DocumentCollection
   (Open, CloseAndDiscard, IsReadOnly), the two attributes -- each forwarding
   to layer 1. Preferably as a THIRD EPURELIB build flavour
   (Framework=clautolisp, #if CLAUTOLISP_APP, next to ARX_APP / BRX_APP)
   rather than assemblies impersonating Autodesk's / Bricsys's names.

* Study questions (why this is DEFERRED)

- *Windows API surface.* Do we support Windows-only dependencies of C# code
  at all, and how far?
  - WinForms dialogs (5 functions): need an STA thread with a message loop
    beside SBCL's main thread (SBCL's thread is not COM-initialized STA);
    modal ownership without a CAD main window. Not available on .NET 8
    macOS / Linux (Mono's WinForms is partial).
  - COM from C#: Word interop for the PDF report; more generally
    out-of-process COM servers. Requires CoInitializeEx and apartment
    rules on the hosting thread.
  - COM from AutoLISP itself: should clautolisp's vlax-create-object reach
    REAL Windows COM (Scripting.FileSystemObject, WinHttp.WinHttpRequest,
    Excel / Word.Application -- all used by AutoLISP corpora) through an
    IDispatch bridge (CoCreateInstance / IDispatch::Invoke via CFFI, or via
    the .NET host's dynamic COM)? That is a sibling feature to this epic and
    shares its threading model; decide jointly.
  - Registry, clipboard, file dialogs, Process: which need shims, which
    just work in .NET.
- *net48 vs net8.* Host unmodified net48 on Windows (mscoree), or require a
  retarget to net8.0 / net8.0-windows (hostfxr, cross-platform)? Costura
  embedding vs net8's deps.json resolution.
- *Shim vs impersonation.* Is a third build flavour acceptable for SCHMS+
  (it is pjb's code), or must unmodified vendor-flavoured DLLs load (needs
  assemblies with Autodesk / Bricsys names and types -- licensing and
  trademark questions)?
- *Reentrancy and threads.* LISP -> C# -> Invoke -> LISP nesting; C# code
  calling back on another thread; error propagation (a .NET exception as a
  LISP error, *error* semantics).
- *Documents.* schms_reouvrir_lecture_seule needs a multi-document host
  (cador-multidocument-host) with read-only open.
- *Value.* For EPUREE, the alternative (epuree user manual, "Three
  trajectories", option B) is reimplementing the ~10 portable functions in
  AutoLISP; .NET hosting pays only if the C# must stay the single source
  for AutoCAD, BricsCAD and clautolisp. Layer 1 has value on its own.

* Acceptance criteria (for the epic, once un-deferred)

- A C plugin built against the layer-1 header registers a LISP function
  that clautolisp calls, with lists / strings / reals / points / nil / T
  round-tripping, on Windows, macOS and Linux.
- (netload "EPURELIB.dll") under clautolisp on Windows makes the pure-.NET
  functions (get_new_guid ... parse_condition_itineraire, ouranos_*)
  callable with the same results as under AutoCAD / BricsCAD; on macOS /
  Linux with a net8 build.
- The study's decisions on WinForms / COM / Word recorded here, with the
  per-platform support matrix in the user manual.

* Scheduling (pjb, 2026-10-05)

"We'll do that after the next release": the study phase starts once the
next clautolisp release is cut.
